[{:adr/authoritative_for ["kotoba-lang/dtn の永続化ストア（:store-path）・バンドル完全性検証（:peer-secrets HMAC）の設計根拠" "「実際に稼働可能」の残りgapのうち、コードで埋められる部分の充足範囲"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "telecom-independent-substrate-dtn-rcs-mesh-satellite", :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607161743-kotoba-lang-rcs-dtn-independent-telecom-substrate.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607161817-kotoba-lang-dtn-tcp-transport-operational.edn" "orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn"], :adr/status :accepted, :adr/id "adr-2607161852-kotoba-lang-dtn-durable-store-bundle-integrity", :adr/doc_type :adr, :adr/last_verified "2026-07-16", :adr/body "---\nid: adr-2607161852-kotoba-lang-dtn-durable-store-bundle-integrity\ntitle: \"ADR-2607161852: kotoba-lang/dtn gains a durable (disk-backed) store and HMAC bundle integrity\"\nstatus: accepted\ndoc_type: adr\ntopic: telecom-independent-substrate-dtn-rcs-mesh-satellite\nauthoritative: true\nlast_verified: 2026-07-16\nauthoritative_for:\n  - kotoba-lang/dtn の永続化ストア（:store-path）・バンドル完全性検証（:peer-secrets HMAC）の設計根拠\n  - 「実際に稼働可能」の残りgapのうち、コードで埋められる部分の充足範囲\nrelated:\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607161743-kotoba-lang-rcs-dtn-independent-telecom-substrate.edn\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607161817-kotoba-lang-dtn-tcp-transport-operational.edn\n  - orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn\nsupersedes: []\nsuperseded_by: []\n---\n\n# ADR-2607161852: kotoba-lang/dtn gains a durable (disk-backed) store and HMAC bundle integrity\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-16\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n## Problem\n\nADR-2607161817 gave `kotoba-lang/dtn` a real internet-overlay TCP transport\nwith genuine cross-process delivery and in-memory store-and-forward. Asked\ndirectly *「残りの gap は?」* after that landed, the orchestrating session\nenumerated the remaining gaps in two categories: environment-blocked\n(mesh-radio/satellite hardware, real carrier gateway credentials, a new\ncloud-itonami actor — none fixable by writing more code here) and\nstill-code-fixable (in-memory-only store, zero transport authentication,\nno multi-hop routing, no peer discovery, no NAT traversal, remaining\nRFC 9171 wire-format details).\n\nOf the code-fixable list, two items directly undercut the design's own\nstated top motivation (disaster/carrier-outage resilience, from\nADR-2607161743's clarifying questions): a node that loses every queued\nmessage on restart isn't meaningfully resilient, and a transport that\naccepts unauthenticated bundles from anyone claiming any source E.164\nisn't meaningfully trustworthy. This ADR closes those two.\n\n## Decision\n\n### Decision 1: durable store — `kotoba.dtn.store`, an append-only EDN log\n\n`src/kotoba/dtn/store.cljc` adds pure (`.cljc`, testable under\n`clojure -M:test`) serialize/deserialize/compact functions for an\nappend-only, newline-delimited `pr-str` EDN log — one bundle per line, the\nsame \"simple, append-only, human-diffable\" shape this workspace already\nuses for its own ledgers (`canvas-ledger.edn`, `fleet-db.ledger.edn`).\n`deserialize-line` returns nil on a blank/malformed line rather than\nthrowing, so a partially-written last line from a crash mid-write doesn't\ncorrupt the whole log on reload. The actual file I/O (`node:fs`) is Node-only,\nbehind a reader-conditional, matching this repo's established `.cljc`\ncore + `.cljs`-only-I/O split.\n\n`kotoba.dtn.transport.tcp/start-node!` gained an **optional** `:store-path`.\nWhen passed: on startup, the on-disk log is loaded into the in-memory\n`:store`; every bundle that falls back to `:store` also gets appended to\ndisk; every successful `retry-store!` pass rewrites the compacted\n(delivered/expired bundles dropped) set back to disk. When omitted,\nbehavior is byte-identical to before (in-memory only) — not a breaking\nchange to the existing demo/CLI callers.\n\n### Decision 2: bundle integrity — `kotoba.dtn.auth`, pre-shared-secret HMAC-SHA256\n\n`src/kotoba/dtn/auth.cljc` adds `sign-bundle`/`verify-bundle` over a\nper-peer pre-shared secret (HMAC-SHA256, `javax.crypto.Mac` on `:clj` /\n`node:crypto` on `:cljs` — same portable-core pattern as Decision 1).\n`kotoba.dtn.transport.tcp/start-node!` gained an **optional**\n`:peer-secrets` map; when a secret is configured for a peer, outbound\nbundles to it are signed and inbound bundles from it are verified before\nbeing admitted to `:inbox` — a bundle that fails verification is logged and\n**dropped, not stored/retried** (a forged/tampered bundle is a security\nevent, not a legitimate delivery worth retrying). Omitted, behavior is\nunchanged from before.\n\nThis is deliberately scoped as **pre-shared-secret origin/tamper checking\nfor a small configured peer set**, not a PKI, not TLS, and explicitly\n**not replay-protected** (no nonce/sequence dedup) — stated plainly in both\nthe namespace docstring and the README, following this repo's existing\n\"claim exactly what you built\" discipline (the same discipline\n`kotoba.dtn.router`'s docstring already uses to disclaim being full CGR).\nA PKI/certificate system and replay protection remain undone, named\nexplicitly rather than silently scoped in or out.\n\n### Decision 3: verify with real re-runs, not the implementing agent's self-report alone\n\nThe demo (`test/kotoba/dtn/transport/tcp_demo.cljs`) gained two more\nscenarios: 4a actually stops a node, \"restarts\" it (fresh `start-node!`\nagainst the same `:store-path`), and asserts the reloaded in-memory store\ncontains the bundle that was there before — proving the persistence\nround-trip against the real file, not just the pure serialize/deserialize\nfunctions in isolation. 4b sends one legitimately-signed message (accepted)\nand one bundle signed with the wrong secret over a raw socket, bypassing\n`send-message!`'s normal signing path (rejected) — proving the transport\nlayer actually enforces verification, not just that `verify-bundle` returns\nthe right boolean in a unit test.\n\nAs with ADR-2607161817, this was independently re-verified by the\norchestrating session from a cold clone before writing this ADR, not\ntrusted from the implementing agent's report alone.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `clojure -M:test` → 26 tests / 112 assertions (was 84; +28 new), 0\n  failures, 0 errors. Independently re-run from a cold clone.\n- `clojure -M:lint` → 0 errors, 0 warnings. Independently re-run.\n- `nbb --classpath \"src:test:../phone/src:../html/src:../css/src\" test/kotoba/dtn/transport/tcp_demo.cljs` → `RESULT: 5/5 scenarios passed`, exit 0 (scenarios 1-3 from ADR-2607161817 unmodified and still passing; new 4a/4b both pass). Independently re-run from a cold clone, output matches the implementing agent's report exactly.\n- Pushed to `github.com/kotoba-lang/dtn` (public), commit `a89edf50cfcc7083f42c2a0446c9e0483a1f6a06`.\n- `manifest/west.yml`: pin advanced via `--entry dtn` (1-line diff, `fdd2b4480f0d→a89edf50cfcc`, `verify-west-pins: 1 件の pin 変更をすべて検証 OK`), landed via an isolated sibling-path worktree + GitHub API server-side merge, matching the two prior ADRs' own landing procedure.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- The two gaps most directly undercutting this design's own resilience\n  premise — volatile store, unauthenticated transport — are closed with\n  real, re-verified code. A node process can now crash and recover its\n  undelivered queue; a peer can no longer inject bundles under a forged\n  source identity without the shared secret.\n- Both additions are additive/optional (`:store-path`, `:peer-secrets`) —\n  zero behavior change for existing callers that don't opt in, so\n  ADR-2607161817's own demo scenarios 1-3 needed no modification.\n- Still explicitly undone, unchanged from the prior gap inventory: no PKI\n  (pre-shared-secret only), no replay protection, no multi-hop routing, no\n  peer discovery (`kotoba-lang/net` gossip composition), no NAT traversal\n  (`kotoba-lang/turn` composition), remaining RFC 9171 wire-format details\n  (CBOR, BPSec, fragmentation), mesh-radio/satellite hardware, real carrier\n  gateway credentials, and a consuming cloud-itonami actor. None of these\n  are silently claimed as done.\n- A durable log that is only compacted on a successful `retry-store!` pass\n  can grow between passes under sustained undeliverable-message load — an\n  known, documented characteristic, not a claimed-away one; no size cap or\n  rotation was added in this ADR.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- **A real embedded database (SQLite, LMDB) instead of an append-only EDN\n  log for the durable store.** Rejected for this scope: the append-only-log\n  shape already matches this workspace's own ledger convention, needs zero\n  new dependencies (still `node:fs` only), and the demo's correctness bar\n  (survive-a-restart) doesn't need transactional query semantics a real DB\n  would add complexity for without benefit here.\n- **A full PKI / certificate-issuance system for bundle authentication.**\n  Rejected: this ADR series has already deferred running-server/\n  key-management-operations concerns to a future consuming actor (per\n  ADR-2607161743 Decision 5); pre-shared-secret HMAC is the honest minimum\n  that closes \"can anyone forge a source identity\" without building an\n  entire CA this scope doesn't need.\n- **Adding replay-attack protection (nonce/sequence dedup) in the same\n  pass.** Rejected for this ADR specifically to keep the two closed gaps\n  cleanly verifiable and scoped; named explicitly as still-undone rather\n  than bundled in partially-done.\n- **Trusting the implementing agent's report without independent\n  re-verification**, again. Rejected for the same reason as\n  ADR-2607161817 — re-run from a cold clone before writing Verification.\n\n## References\n\n- `90-docs/adr/2607161743-kotoba-lang-rcs-dtn-independent-telecom-substrate.edn`\n- `90-docs/adr/2607161817-kotoba-lang-dtn-tcp-transport-operational.edn`\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn/README.edn` — https://github.com/kotoba-lang/dtn\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn/src/kotoba/dtn/store.cljc`\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn/src/kotoba/dtn/auth.cljc`\n", :adr/artifacts "{:kotoba-lang-dtn \"kotoba-lang/dtn @ a89edf50cfcc (pushed, public)\", :manifest \"orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn pin advanced via --entry dtn, pin-verified\"}", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607161852: kotoba-lang/dtn gains a durable (disk-backed) store and HMAC bundle integrity", :adr/source-format "edn"}]